      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I am slowly turning crazy over this issue, since I instantly get an error when trying to play either Twitch or VRCDN links over ProTV.\n\nYouTube Videos and Livestreams work without issues.\n\nAn exempt of the error log can be found underneath.\n\nHardware:\n\nCPU: Intel i7700k\n\nGPU: GTX1070\n\nRAM: 32GB\n\nEverything like reinstalling the game, turning off my firewall e.g. didn't bring any success.\n\nAt this point I am at a completely fresh Windows 10 install with no system parameters whatsoever changed.\n\nLog:\n\n2024.10.14 14:34:53 Log        -  NativeProcess.HasExited: process exited with code 1, took 2268 ms. Command line: C:/Users/tobia/AppData/LocalLow/VRChat/VRChat\\Tools/yt-dlp.exe (...)\n\n2024.10.14 14:34:53 Error      -  [Video Playback] ERROR: [twitch:stream] onibabakosushitokyo_: Failed to download m3u8 information: [SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: unable to get local issuer certificate (_ssl.c:1131) (caused by CertificateVerifyError('[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: unable to get local issuer certificate (_ssl.c:1131)')); please report this issue on  https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/issues?q= , filling out the appropriate issue template. Confirm you are on the latest version using  yt-dlp -U\n\n2024.10.14 14:34:53 Log        -  [Video Playback] URL 'https://www.twitch.tv/onibabakosushitokyo_' resolved to 'https://www.twitch.tv/onibabakosushitokyo_'\n\n2024.10.14 14:34:53 Log        -  [AVProVideo] Opening https://www.twitch.tv/onibabakosushitokyo_ (offset 0) with API MediaFoundation\n\n2024.10.14 14:34:53 Error      -  [AVProVideo] Error: Loading failed.  File not found, codec not supported, video resolution too high or insufficient system resources.\n\n2024.10.14 14:34:53 Error      -  [USharpVideo] Video player error when trying to load https://www.twitch.tv/onibabakosushitokyo_\n\nArchitech (ProTV DEV) confirmed that it is a YT-DLP issue, I just want to listen to DJs again. :(",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
