  "details": "Beginning in the latest update and/or around 10/4/24, Twitch links plugging into (at least) the AVPro and/or TXL video players results in around 1/10th of PCVR players unable to hear audio or see the Twitch stream. Instead, they see \"VIDEO ERROR\" on the screen immediately after the link is plugged in. I cannot replicate this issue myself but it appears to be affecting users all over the world on PCVR only. It is affecting people in PCVR specifically (but maybe also on desktop, I am unsure) regardless of internet speed, PC build, GPU, video player custom launch options, etc. It does not appear to be affecting Quest users. By using a VRCDN link, it circumvents this issue but VRCDN is a paid service and not all can afford it or know how to use it. \n\nPlease let me know if you need anymore information. I can also direct you to users who are experiencing this problem or ask them for more information.",
